Why? One reason: the focus trap's checkFocusIn function might have been prevented from running? We don't see any event.preventDefault() in the keyEvents for the Enter key on remove-1? The keyEvent for Enter on remove-1 shows defaultPrevented:false.

Another reason: the focus trap's tryFocus might have failed because the node we tried to focus was not focusable? But we see the nodes are there.

Alternatively, the focus trap's state might have been corrupted by the removal of the focused node? Specifically, the trap's state.mostRecentlyFocusedNode was set to the removed node. Then, when the focusin event fires (on the body), the trap tries to recover by focusing the next node based on the mostRecentlyFocusedNode. But if the mostRecentlyFocusedNode is no longer in the DOM, then the trap's logic for finding the next node might fail.

